{"author":{"id":"a3a282966ced55effb4560271fcd98e13241af24ea76b00ec76a0f18154bc8ee"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790964355,"nonce":"xYdQbckPvWd2VIATo2+b9HlemVM=","message":"Landed. The three pages' `body` now returns, alongside its lines, a parallel\n`[]int` saying which line each line's `group_by` header is drawn on (-1 where\nthere is none), and one shared helper, `window` in `tui/list_view.go`, picks\nthe lines the page draws: it calls `scroll` as before, and then, when the\nwindow opens on a line that is not itself a header, puts that line's group\nheader on the window's first line and the rows from `top+1` under it. The\ncursor can never end up behind the sticky line: when the scroll put it on the\nfirst line, `top` moves one line up, which either frees a line under the header\nor lands on the header itself, where nothing is sticky. A one-line window keeps\nno sticky header, the cursor's row wins it.\n\nThe sticky line is the header as the page already drew it, so what it carries\ncomes with it: the gantt's crosshair and group tint, the board's per-lane line.\n`rowsPerPage` / `cardsPerPage` are untouched.\n\nTests, one per kind (`TestGroupedListKeepsTheGroupHeaderOnTop`,\n`TestGroupedBoardKeepsTheLaneHeaderOnTop`, `TestGroupedGanttKeepsTheGroupHeaderOnTop`):\nwith a window too small for the body and three groups, scrolled to the end the\nwindow opens on the second group's header over rows that are not the group's\nfirst, and back up on that group's first row the header is still the first body\nline with the cursor's row right under it; the cursor's row is on screen in\nboth, and the gantt asserts the sticky line is the header line crosshair and\nall. All three fail without the change.\n\nDoc: `doc/design/terminal-renderer.md`, under Navigation and editing, records\nthe decision and why — a header off the scroll window is unreachable, since the\nscroll follows the cursor and the cursor cannot stand on a header, and the top\nrows lose their label; AGENTS.md gets one sentence in the view-keys paragraph.","files":null}]}